    "name": "Shishito Frying Pepper",
    "description": "<p>Shishitos are bright, flavorful sweet chilies with typically mild spiciness. There's a fiery punch every so often where a shishito breaks the norm and turns up the dial. It makes them a ton of fun to eat. Cook them up as a side or a fun appetizer. Shishitos range from 100 to 1,000 Scoville heat units, which is hotter than bell peppers but much milder than jalapenos.</p>",
